            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.071,
            0.494,
            0.089
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.11,
            0.882,
            0.189
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Notice that the final concentration is not the simple average of 10% and 20%. It is closer to 10% because the larger quantity of lemonade comes from the 10% mixture. In general, each concentration influences the final concentration according to the quantity of mixture it contributes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.192,
            0.882,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 5:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Brass is an alloy of copper and zinc. Batch A of brass weighs 200 kg of which 70% is copper. Batch B weighs 120 kg of which 50% is copper. Batch C is 45% copper. When all three batches are combined, we get an alloy that is 55% copper. What is the weight of Batch C?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.268,
            0.744,
            0.288
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The concentration of copper in the mixture is given by"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.293,
            0.68,
            0.336
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac { \\quad \\quad \\quad \\quad \\quad \\quad \\quad q u a n t i t y \\quad o f c o p p e r \\quad i n \\quad t h e \\quad m i x t u r e \\quad } { q u a n t i t y \\quad o f t h e \\quad m i x t u r e \\quad } \\cdot"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.339,
            0.881,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose y is the weight (in kg) of Batch C. From the given information, we know that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.387,
            0.876,
            0.427
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "0.55 = \\frac{(Quanity   of   cosp per   in   Bach   A + Qunity   of   cosp per   in   Bacth   B + Qunity   of   cdp   per   in   Bacth   C)}{Total   weignt   of   br a s   in   all   batch   s}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.323,
            0.433,
            0.713,
            0.527
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}0.55 = \\frac{200 \\times 0.7 + 120 \\times 0.5 + y \\times 0.45}{200 + 120 + y} \\cdot \\\\0.55(320 + y) = 200 + 0.45y. \\\\y = 240.\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.528,
            0.364,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Batch C weighs 240 kg."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.548,
            0.881,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "More generally, if n things with concentrations "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X _ { 1 } ,   X _ { 2 } ,   X _ { 3 } ,   \\ldots   ,   X _ { n }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and respective volumes/weights "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w_{1},w_{2},w_{3},\\ldots,w_{n}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are mixed, the concentration of the mixture is given by"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.319,
            0.619,
            0.677,
            0.664
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "\\chi = \\frac{W_{1}X_{1} + W_{2}X_{2} + W_{3}X_{3} + \\cdots + W_{n}X_{n}}{W_{1} + W_{2} + W_{3} + \\cdots + W_{n}}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.67,
            0.882,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Such an average is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "weighted mean",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "weighted average",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Here, the prefix ‘weighted’ does not refer to actual weights but abstract weights; however, in some cases, these can be actual weights. That is, the weighted mean is an average where each value is weighted (multiplied) by how important or how big it is. We shall study other contexts where the weighted average is used."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.782,
            0.883,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The above formula for the weighted mean was written down by Brahmagupta in his work Brāhmasphuṭasiddhānta (c. 628 CE). He used the formula to define the mean depth x of an irregularly-shaped pit. If the pit has depth measurement "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x _ { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for length "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w _ { _ 1 } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " depth measurement "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for length "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w _ { 2 ^ { \\flat } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " … and depth measurement "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X _ { n }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for length "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "w _ { n ^ { \\flat } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then the mean depth x is given by the above formula."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
